# TypeScript comment style

Never use JSDoc / block documentation comments that start with `/**`.

This applies to single-line and multi-line forms alike. Prefer `//` for
ordinary comments, including multi-line notes (one `//` per line). Plain
`/* ... */` is also avoided for documentation; use `//` instead.

```ts
// ❌ BAD
/** Encode a timestamp for the wire. */
export function encodeUsTimestamp(us: bigint): string { ... }

/**
 * Shared WebSocket contract.
 * Timestamps are decimal strings.
 */
export type UsTimestampString = string;

// ✅ GOOD
// Encode a timestamp for the wire.
export function encodeUsTimestamp(us: bigint): string { ... }

// Shared WebSocket contract.
// Timestamps are decimal strings.
export type UsTimestampString = string;
```
